- 2026-10-05 glass shadow clip: a GlassShadow with an offset shadow clips
  its shadows to outside the shape (an even-odd path of the shadow bounds
  and the shape deflated by half a pixel) instead of drawing them into a
  saveLayer and cutting the shape out with dstOut: no offscreen pass per
  shadowed surface, no shadow under the glass; only the antialiasing at
  the cut differs (flutter_test: <= 1 channel off the edge,
  test/glass_body_shadow_test.dart).
- 2026-10-05 live shapes and layers: LiquidGlass.live (a ValueListenable
  of LiquidGlassShapeFrame: shape, appearance, shadows) and
  LiquidGlassLayer.live (a Listenable with settingsOf / fieldOf) write each
  new frame straight into their render objects (RenderLiquidGlass, the
  glass shadow, the shape clip and visibility opacity, RenderFakeGlass,
  RenderLiquidGlassLayer, RenderConsolidatedFakeGlassLayer) through the
  GlassLiveBinding mixin (internal/glass_live.dart): the setters decide
  what changed, no widget rebuilds. The layer's scope carries the live
  settings (LiquidGlassRenderScope.settingsLive / currentSettings) for the
  shapes below it. A live shape rebuilds only when its kind of shape
  changes or its shadows appear or vanish; configurations no render
  object can follow (a standalone fake shape) rebuild per frame
  (GlassRebuildOn). GlassContentSource takes the same notifications to
  record its content again while a lens captures. The fixed constructors
  are unchanged and the same render objects are built either way, so the
  pixels are the same (test/glass_frames_test.dart).
- 2026-10-05 pipeline warm-up: internal/glass_warm_up.dart (new) draws
  every Flutter GPU pipeline of the geometry passes once (two 8 x 8
  renders through FlutterGpuGeometryRenderer.render) and rasterizes an
  offscreen layer scene with each final shader's backdrop filter (alone
  and composed over a mirror blur) and the frosted tier's blurs, clips,
  decorations and shadows, so the first glass frame creates no pipeline.
  Called from morphPrecacheLiquidGlass; failures are swallowed. No
  renderer source changed.
- 2026-10-05 fake glass as morph's fake tier (the frosted tier removed):
  internal/fake_glass_color.dart fits the face transfer's luminance line
  exact at black (least squares over (0, 1]) instead of over [0, 1],
  which lifted black by lift / 6; ConsolidatedFakeGlassLayer draws a
  fused body's regions with the face of their largest shape only (the
  others clipped outside it) and its neck as the outline clipped outside
  every shape (no even-odd double tint); LiquidGlassLayer.live takes an
  `outlineOf` for a body fused without a field (a plain union), which
  only the fake path reads. The warm-up's frosted scene became the fake
  glass scene: the face matrix alone and over each frost, both clips, the
  fake surface shader.
- 2026-10-05 exterior decode: decodeSignedEdgeDistance
  (shaders/gpu/displacement_encoding.glsl) selects inward or exterior
  range with step() arithmetic instead of a ternary; the Vulkan pipeline
  on Mali-G78 evaluated the ternary's exterior branch as 0 inside the
  full final shader and drew half the glass over the whole filter clip.
  Bit-identical result elsewhere (glass-renderer.md, Vulkan exterior
  boxes).
- 2026-10-05 uniform arena: internal/flutter_gpu_geometry_renderer_native
  .dart replaces the shared Flutter GPU HostBuffer with MorphUniformArena,
  a bump allocator over hostVisible DeviceBuffers that never lets an
  emplacement cross a block end (HostBuffer checks only the start, so the
  ~32nd uniform write of a frame failed and its layer was not drawn) and
  reuses a frame slot's extra blocks. debugHostBufferBlockLength /
  debugHostBufferIdentity became debugUniformBlockLength /
  debugUniformArenaIdentity (also in the web stub).
- 2026-10-05 32 shapes per layer: MAX_SHAPES 16 -> 32 in
  shaders/gpu/geometry_fragment.glsl, sdf.glsl and
  material_gradient_fragment.glsl (materialShapeTint's chain to 31), the
  final shader's contributor decode (x 32, clamp 31), and on the Dart side
  FlutterGpuGeometryRenderer.maxShapes (uniform packing, appearance rows,
  the material map's minimum width, the layer's shape cap, the warm-up's
  appearance data). The geometry uniforms grow from 2352 bytes; a layer of
  16 shapes or fewer draws the same pixels (Pixel 6a density shots, 0
  difference).
- 2026-10-05 shader audit batch (tool/audit/shader-audit-*.md; numbers in
  glass-renderer.md, Shader harness): liquid_glass_final_render_core.glsl
  computes the border coverage and its light direction once, returns the
  face unlit past the glint, the inner border and the bevel band, picks the
  color model shares, the glint's return weight and the contributor pair
  repair with 0/1 step weights, fetches each palette row once when both
  contributors are one shape, and skips pow for an exponent of exactly 1
  (wrap 0.5, gamma 1); fake_glass_surface.frag runs in highp (on Vulkan its
  mediump put the silhouette in fp16 on Mali), returns the border ring
  outside the clip without the material, and skips the same pow;
  fake_glass_shape.glsl tests the cap span by cosine instead of atan. Tried
  and reverted because a device moved pixels the proposal called identical:
  sharing the decoded matte normal with decodeDisplacement and a
  step-weighted normal decode (Mali, an ulp in the displacement), the
  exterior reject ahead of the material map (Metal, material variant).
  ShaderKeys.debugRuntimeRoot lets the harness load a frozen copy of the
  runtime shaders (example/shader_audit/baseline).
- 2026-10-06 layer hygiene: RenderLiquidGlassLayer keeps the tracked
  screen transform without a copy (the shader transform copies it only
  when the pass transform changes it), inverts the coordinate mapping into
  a kept matrix and maps its points with MatrixUtils.transformPoint's
  arithmetic, writes the mapping and sampled-bounds uniforms with
  setFloat, compares shape appearances in place, and keeps the frost blur
  per sigma. The same uniforms and filters as before (glass_frames on the
  host's Impeller).
- 2026-10-06 filter census: the painters that keep a backdrop filter in a
  private handle (the layer's shader, the fake layer's, the opacity seed)
  note it with `GlassLayerOwners` when a census asks (null otherwise); the
  debug warning about an Opacity between a shape and its layer fires only
  for one below 1 (a MorphTag's opacity is exactly 1 while it shows).
- 2026-10-06 frost seed: LiquidGlassLayer.blursOwnBackdrop (set by the
  widget layer on lifted lens, knob and thumb glass): while the frost needs
  a blur pass and the layer is outside a backdrop group and an opacity
  seed, the material filter is pushed under a clip of its filter clip grown
  by the blur's reach and an identity color-filter backdrop, so the
  composed blur reads that pass instead of the whole enclosing one; the
  shader's pass origin is that pass's (shaderCoordinateTransform).
  `RenderLiquidGlassLayer.debugSeedsBlur` turns it off for an A/B. Numbers
  in glass-renderer.md ("The lifted lens's frost").
- 2026-10-06 Mali offline compiler batch (numbers in glass-renderer.md,
  "The Mali offline compiler batch"): the final shader's one-appearance
  and tint-only entry points compile one color model family each
  (DIRECT_MODEL or IOS27_MODELS: liquid_glass_final_render(_tint).frag and
  the new liquid_glass_final_render(_tint)_ios27.frag); the material
  variant keeps both. RenderLiquidGlassLayer holds five final shaders and
